// Shumway debugger - registration that the [Provide*] attributes cannot express.
//
// A TextMate grammar REPOSITORY: VS scans the folder, reads each grammar's own fileTypes,
// and colours those extensions. That is the whole .pl colorizer -- no editor factory, no
// language service, no content type.
[$RootKey$\TextMate\Repositories]
"Shumway"="$PackageFolder$\Grammars"

// The NAME of the language, for the Call Stack window's Language column (and everywhere else
// Visual Studio prints one). Our frames carry a DkmCompilerId -- a (language, vendor) pair of
// GUIDs -- and that is all Concord needs to route the expression evaluator. But a GUID is not
// a name: with nothing registered here the Call Stack said "unknown", which is a fair summary
// of what the IDE knew about it.
//
// The key is (language GUID, vendor GUID), matching ShumwayGuids.ShumwayLanguage and
// ShumwayGuids.ShumwayVendor. Do not let these drift apart: nothing fails, the column just
// goes back to saying "unknown".
[$RootKey$\AD7Metrics\ExpressionEvaluator\{9d7f8a51-0699-4828-99ba-047821c60783}\{026ae3f6-168e-448c-9518-4ac5d49ce8d1}]
"Language"="Prolog"
"Name"="Prolog"
